<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">USS Charleston (C-2)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">USS Charleston was a protected cruiser of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-navy">United States Navy</a>, commissioned in 1889. In June 1898, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, she entered Apra Harbour on Guam and fired on the old fort; the Spanish governor, unaware that war had been declared, surrendered the island without a fight. She was wrecked off the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1899.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uss-charleston-c-2.jpg" alt="USS Charleston (C-2)" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USS_CHARLESTON_(C-2).tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
